# PROFILE.example — the skillpipe instance file (host-bound)

The repo carries doctrine with this example; the FILLED instance lives
host-side (one per install) and is NOT committed here. Copy it, fill every
key, and point the operator at it via the `SKILLPIPE_INSTANCE`
environment variable or the `--instance` flag.

This is the ONE place host-bound values live: repo paths, the GitHub repo
slug, the board name, the role profiles. The doctrine (this skill, the
playbooks, the script) is host-neutral and references the instance by
token only.

## Required keys

```
# Absolute path to the house skill repo checkout (the main worktree, on
# main, clean). The pipeline reads CONVENTIONS.md and the linter from
# here; intake refuses to run if the TARGET SKILL DIR is dirty on main.
REPO_DIR=/abs/path/to/hermes-skills

# The GitHub repo slug the issues and PRs live in (gh --repo).
REPO=owner/hermes-skills

# The kanban board the dispatch cards are created on.
BOARD=skills

# Parent dir for one worktree per in-flight pipeline. intake creates
# <WORKTREE_ROOT>/<skill> on branch sr/<skill>; merge removes it.
WORKTREE_ROOT=/abs/path/to/hermes-skills-worktrees

# The directory holding the six role playbooks (<role>-role.md). The
# script asserts the playbook exists before it dispatches a role.
CARDS_DIR=/abs/path/to/skill-kanban/references

# Who runs the cards. Single-runner install: one profile name (every role
# runs as it). Role-isolated install: a role=profile map — one profile +
# one memory bank per role severs the backchannel between adversarial
# roles (an auditor must not recall what the author it is checking
# reasoned).
ASSIGNEE=author=sr-author, audit=sr-audit, ste100=sr-ste100, scripter=sr-scripter, verifier=sr-verifier, commit=sr-commit, fleet=sr-fleet
```

## Optional keys

```
# Model pin for the drafting roles (author, scripter). Leave unset to run
# those roles on the profile default. Judging roles (audit, ste100,
# verifier, commit, fleet) always run on the profile default.
MID_MODEL=qwen-27b-agentic

# The house-repo skill force-loaded on every card (the rubric + linter).
HOUSE_SKILL=hermes-skills-repo

# The controlled-language writing standard force-loaded on the ste100 card
# only (next to the house skill).
STD_SKILL=asd-ste100

# The pinned linter toolkit for style-check: a venv with pycodestyle,
# pyflakes and isort plus a shellcheck binary (bin/). The style-check verb
# refuses to run without it — the standard is enforced or the gap is
# reported, never silently skipped.
STYLE_TOOLKIT=/abs/path/to/skillpipe-style

# The profile recorded as the creator on every dispatch card.
CREATED_BY=skillpipe

# Per-role runtime caps (default 30m). Long scans (ste100, verifier)
# benefit from more; these are the only knobs for that.
RUNTIME_AUTHOR=30m
RUNTIME_AUDIT=30m
RUNTIME_STE100=45m
RUNTIME_SCRIPTER=45m
RUNTIME_VERIFIER=1h
RUNTIME_COMMIT=40m
RUNTIME_FLEET=30m
```

## Worked example (role-isolated install)

```
REPO_DIR=/home/user/hermes-skills
REPO=user/hermes-skills
BOARD=skills
WORKTREE_ROOT=/home/user/hermes-skills-worktrees
CARDS_DIR=/home/user/hermes-skills/skill-kanban/references
ASSIGNEE=author=sr-author, audit=sr-audit, ste100=sr-ste100, \
  scripter=sr-scripter, verifier=sr-verifier, commit=sr-commit, fleet=sr-fleet
MID_MODEL=<your-mid-tier-model-id>
HOUSE_SKILL=hermes-skills-repo
STD_SKILL=asd-ste100
CREATED_BY=skillpipe
STYLE_TOOLKIT=/home/user/tools/skillpipe-style
```

## Notes

- One pipeline per skill in flight: `intake` refuses a second pipeline for
  a skill that already has an open issue. Different skills run in parallel
  (separate worktrees).
- The state machine is the script, not the doctrine: the transition table,
  the loop caps, and the park labels all live in `skillpipe.py` and are
  covered by `skillpipe_test.py` (run by CI and the pre-push hook). If a
  label or cap changes, it changes there and in the test together.
- The filled instance is host-bound by design. Do not commit it; the repo
  keeps only this example.
